  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Codes never in JWTs",
      "items": [
        "6-digit codes are single-use, capped at 5 wrong guesses (subtle.ConstantTimeCompare), and expire in 24h; resets run 30m with a 3-per-5-min per-email rate limit",
        "re-signup of an unverified email re-issues the code and re-enqueues the mail (201); a verified email answers 409 AUTH_EMAIL_TAKEN",
        "reset answers auto-verify the account and default to revoking all sessions (<APP>_LOGOUT_ALL_ON_RESET)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Gates",
      "items": [
        "the password verifies FIRST — one constant 401 AUTH_INVALID_CREDENTIALS and retry_count++ even on gated accounts, so no probe can infer account state",
        "state gates run only after the password verifies: inactive → blocked → unverified, each a stable 403 code",
        "bcrypt cost 10 over base64(HMAC-SHA256(password, <APP>_PASSWORD_PEPPER)); empty pepper means disabled, not zeroed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Tokens",
      "items": [
        "access JWT HS256 15m: sub · email · role · jti · iat · exp · iss (golang-jwt/jwt/v5); refresh is opaque base64url 48B",
        "refresh rotates in place under a compare-and-swap on the presented token (jti keeps matching; absolute expires_at never slides)",
        "a replayed refresh misses the CAS (0 rows) → ErrInvalidRefresh 401 — nothing is minted"
      ]
    }
  ]
}